A slideshow file (the "slides.*" resources, and the files of "call"
commands) lists the commands of a cutscene:

{
  "version": 1,
  "commands": [
    {"comment": "Set size", "op": "dims", "width": 320, "height": 240},
    {"op": "ani", "resolution": "sd", "file": "base/cutscene/intro/intro.ani.json"},
    {"op": "draw", "frame": 0}
  ]
}

"comment" is optional, and the game does not use it. "resolution" ("sd"
or "hd") is optional: a command for the other resolution does nothing.
Positions and sizes are in SD pixels. Times are in milliseconds.

dims              width, height: size of the slideshow, centered on screen
font              index (0 to 4), file (optional): load a font into a slot,
                  and use the font of the slot
ani               file: the animation file to draw frames from
music             file: play a music file
ditty             ship: play the ditty of a ship, "ship.<ship>.ditty"
call              file: show another slideshow file
wait              ms: wait, or until a key skips it
spinWait          ms: wait during a ship spin
waitDitty         wait until the ditty ends
sync              ms: wait until this time from the start
resync            make the current time the start
deltaSync         ms: wait until this time from the last sync
fadeToColor       ms: fade the screen in
fadeToBlack       ms: fade the screen to black
fadeToWhite       ms: fade the screen to white
clearScreen       clear the screen
backgroundColor   color [r, g, b]: background color of the context
textColor         color [r, g, b]: color of the text
textBackColor     color [r, g, b]: back color of the text
textFadeColor     color [r, g, b]: color that text fades from and to
textAlign         align ("top", "middle", "bottom"): position of faded text
textEffect        effect ("plain", "traced")
text              x, y, text: draw centered text
textFadeIn        lines (1 to 15): fade in lines of text
textFadeOut       fade out the text of the last textFadeIn
textSpin          x, y, text: draw text of a ship spin
spinStat          filled, empty, text: draw a stat line in the stat box
statBox           x, y: draw the stat box of a ship spin
lineSpin          x1, y1, x2, y2: draw a line of a ship spin
line              x1, y1, x2, y2: draw a line
getRect           remember the bounds of the last frame drawn; the spin
                  commands are relative to them
draw              frame, x, y, scale, angle: draw a frame of the animation.
                  x and y are optional (0, 0). scale (256 = 1x) needs x and
                  y, and angle (degrees) needs scale.
drawSis           x, y, scale, angle: draw the flagship with its modules
saveBackground    copy the screen to a second buffer
restoreBackground copy the second buffer back to the screen
batch, unbatch    batch the drawing commands between them
movie             fps, from, to: show frames of the animation as a movie
animate           first, last, loops, ms, fps: loop frames of the animation

scripts/convert_slideshows.py converts the old string table slideshows,
which have one command line such as "DRAW 3 10 20" in each string, to this
format.

This information is parsed in uqm/slideshow.cpp.
